{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>And if water be put upon seed.</b> After it has been kneaded — for if you should say there is hikhshur while attached, there is no seed that has not been hukhshar (Ḥullin 118)." "<b>Water upon seed.</b> Whether water or other liquids, whether they are upon the seed or the seed falls into them — all is expounded in Torat Kohanim." "<b>And any part of their carcass falls upon it.</b> Even after it has dried from the water — for the Torah was insistent only that the name 'food' be upon it. And once the hikhshur for receiving impurity has come upon it once, it is never again uprooted from it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:58.717434317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}